# A face-down permanent that becomes a copy of another permanent is that permanent's copy once it is turned face up, and
# the copy effect ends with its duration as on any other permanent (CR 708.8, 708.10, 707.2, 611.2b). While it is face
# down it is still a nameless 2/2: its face-down status applies after the copy effect (CR 613.2b).
#
# Turn 1 is the Abhorrent Oculus opening of the other manifest scenarios, with Mirrorweave and Mox Pearl among the cards
# Wheel of Fortune draws (and Forest and Haywire Mite among Bot2's). On Bot2's upkeep the Oculus manifests dread:
# Snapcaster Mage goes onto the battlefield face down, and Bot2 casts Haywire Mite. On Bot1's turn 3 Mirrorweave makes
# each other creature a copy of the Mite until end of turn, the face-down Mage among them; the Mage is then turned face
# up for {1}{U}, and it is a Haywire Mite, a 1/1, not a Snapcaster Mage. As the turn ends Mirrorweave's effect ends,
# and it is a Snapcaster Mage, a 2/1, not a face-down 2/2.

